  "summary": "Boeing 747 cargo flight crashed shortly after takeoff when improperly secured heavy vehicles shifted aft during climb, damaging hydraulic systems and the horizontal stabilizer, causing pitch-up, stall, and impact.",
  "probable_cause": "National Airlines' inadequate procedures for restraining special cargo loads resulted in the loadmaster's improper restraint of the cargo, which moved aft and damaged hydraulic systems Nos. 1 and 2 and horizontal stabilizer drive mechanism components, rendering the airplane uncontrollable.",
